{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00893",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 2.2,
      "end_seconds": 16.28,
      "duration_seconds": 14.08,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm Amrit's wife. A colleague told him his eyes look yellow, and I'm worried about it, so I made him come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.88,
      "end_seconds": 29.17,
      "duration_seconds": 10.29,
      "text": "You were right to come. Mr Dhillon, when did you or anyone first notice the yellow in your eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.6,
      "end_seconds": 42.16,
      "duration_seconds": 9.56,
      "text": "A colleague mentioned it on Monday, but I think it was there before. I wasn't looking."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 44.5,
      "end_seconds": 55.72,
      "duration_seconds": 11.22,
      "text": "I noticed his eyes were a bit yellow about two weeks ago, but I thought it was the lighting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.74,
      "end_seconds": 66.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "So somewhere between a few days and two weeks. Have you noticed dark urine or pale stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.19,
      "end_seconds": 76.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "The urine has been dark, like tea. I didn't think about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.69,
      "end_seconds": 82.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Any itching, tummy pain or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.24,
      "end_seconds": 88.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "No itching. No pain. No fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 90.96,
      "end_seconds": 94.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "He's been very tired, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.86,
      "end_seconds": 103.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "How much alcohol do you drink, Mr Dhillon?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.87,
      "end_seconds": 113.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "A couple of whiskies on a Friday night, no more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.46,
      "end_seconds": 120.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Are you taking any regular medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.6,
      "end_seconds": 129.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Just the blood pressure tablet, amlodipine, 5 mg, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 132.31,
      "end_seconds": 140.14,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "Doctor, do you want me to take his observations and set up for bloods? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.02,
      "end_seconds": 153.46,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "Yes, please. Pulse, pressure, temperature, and we'll take blood for liver tests and a full blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 157.32,
      "end_seconds": 162.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Of course. Mr Dhillon, if you'd roll up your sleeve. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.16,
      "end_seconds": 178.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 181.91,
      "end_seconds": 187.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Pulse 78, blood pressure 130 over 82, temperature 36.8."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 190.45,
      "end_seconds": 192.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Are those normal? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.68,
      "end_seconds": 206.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.6,
      "text": "They're fine. What worries me is the yellow colour, and your dark urine, which could be a liver or bile duct problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.18,
      "end_seconds": 212.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Is it serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.65,
      "end_seconds": 226.99,
      "duration_seconds": 11.34,
      "text": "It can be, and that's why I want the blood tests today, and an ultrasound scan of your liver as soon as we can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 230.95,
      "end_seconds": 233.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "How soon? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.0,
      "end_seconds": 246.01,
      "duration_seconds": 10.01,
      "text": "I'll ask for it this week. I'll phone you with the blood results as soon as they're back. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.76,
      "end_seconds": 251.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I'd rather know quickly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.18,
      "end_seconds": 261.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "Of course, and I'll make sure the lab marks the sample as urgent. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 264.81,
      "end_seconds": 268.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Thank you, we appreciate that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.73,
      "end_seconds": 284.2,
      "duration_seconds": 12.47,
      "text": "I understand. If your skin gets more yellow, you become feverish with pain, or you can't keep fluids down, go to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 287.67,
      "end_seconds": 291.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "We'll watch for that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.06,
      "end_seconds": 298.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Please avoid alcohol completely until we know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.66,
      "end_seconds": 306.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I will. Thank you, doctor. ~"
    }
  ]
}
